      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      }, {
        "name" : "Software"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-82181",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-82181"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "treatment protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0003969"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "After differentiation, the medium was replaced by IMDM culture medium without M-CSF and supplemented with the following stimuli: nothing, 10ng/mL LPS (Sigma, E. coli E55:O5), 10ng/mL LPS plus 50ng/mL IFNγ (R&D), 50ng/mL IFNγ, 50ng/mL IL4 (PeproTech), 50ng/mL IL10 (R&D), 100nM dexamethasone (Sigma) for 24 hours. LPSearly macrophages were first cultured with culture medium for 21 hours and then stimulated with 10ng/mL LPS for 3 hours prior to harvest."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      }, {
        "name" : "Software"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-82180",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-82180"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "growth protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0003789"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were isolated through density centrifugation using Lymphoprep™ (Axis-Shield, Dundee, Scotland). Monocytes were purified through human CD14 magnetic beads and the MACS® cell separation columns (Miltenyi, Bergisch Gladbach, Germany). The resulting monocytes were seeded on 24-well tissue culture plates at a density of 0.8 million cells/well. Cells were subsequently differentiated to macrophages for 6 days in the presence of 50ng/mL human M-CSF (Miltenyi, Germany) with Iscove's Modified Dulbecco's Medium (IMDM) containing 10% heat-inactivated fetal bovine serum (FCS), 1% Penicillin/Streptomycin solution (Gibco) and 1% L-glutamine solution (Gibco). The medium was renewed on the third day."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      }, {
        "name" : "Software"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-82186",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-82186"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "high throughput sequence alignment protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0004917"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "All raw fastq files were first checked for quality using FastQC (v0.11.7)  and MultiQC (v1.4). The sequencing reads were aligned against the human genome GRCh38 using STAR (v2.5.4). Post-alignment processing was performed using SAMtools (v1.7) after which reads overlapping gene features obtained from Ensembl (v91) were counted using the featureCounts  program in the Subread (v1.6.1) package."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware",
        "value" : "Dell T8310"
      }, {
        "name" : "Software",
        "value" : "STAR"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-82185",
